   1354  fc38							; VCS3 — OvShutScan body (Phase C kill test; bank2 tramp `sta $1FF9 / jmp
   1355  fc38							; $FD80` at $FE48). IN: A = kill clock (EnemyRamP-1), Y = MetaB b6 hot bit
   1356  fc38							; ($40/0 — staged bank2-side; MetaB lives in bank2 models_data ROM, a
   1357  fc38							; (RoomPF0Lo),Y fetch here would see bank3's pad). OUT (2026-10-14b):
   1358  fc38							; C=0 passable (A ignored) / C=1 + A≠0 kill / C=1 + A=0 SOLID block —
   1359  fc38							; returned through the $FBEE pad (sta $1FF8 executed here, rts fetched
   1360  fc38							; from bank2's byte-identical copy) to OvShutBand's jsr — A and C
   1361  fc38							; survive both; X/Y clobbered (OvShutBand reloads A before the latch).
   1362  fc38							; Kill semantics (user spec 2026-10-14, superseded the 2026-10-13
   1363  fc38							; endpoint-only rule): a horizontal containment gate (after the clock
   1364  fc38							; math, before the hot/cold split) — the player's lit span must sit
   1365  fc38							; inside the column [BallX-7, BallX] or the call returns passable
   1366  fc38							; (side brush, user bug 2026-10-14: touching the closed block from the
   1367  fc38							; side is not a crunch). Then hot band (MetaB b6) = touching ANY
   1368  fc38							; closed slice kills (endpoint test ≡ any-part: the ping-pong states
   1369  fc38							; $11/$1B/$1F never have a closed middle with open ends). Cold band =
   1370  fc38							; containment only: kill iff the whole sprite sits inside CLOSED
   1371  fc38							; slices (crunched) — $1F trivially; $1B/$11 iff the box misses the
   1372  fc38							; aperture (H≥gapHi or F<gapLo). Touching an edge from the open side
   1373  fc38							; is not a cold kill — that is what the hot flag is for. Every
   1374  fc38							; NON-kill outcome (side brush, opening half, totally closed, the
   1375  fc38							; aperture at the player's Y) goes through the solidity test
   1376  fc38							; (.V3solidBody): both endpoints open → passable, else SOLID block —
   1377  fc38							; the punched cell must not be walkable through a closed shutter
   1378  fc38							; (user 2026-10-14b).
   1379  fc38							; Clock parity: RefreshEnemyY inc'd EnemyRamP at overscan entry, so
   1380  fc38							; clock-1 = the exact value the kernel rendered slices from this frame.
   1381  fc38							; Endpoints: RoomY (head) + RoomY+11 (feet = PLAYER_SPRITE_H-1) — every
   1382  fc38							; open state's gap is >=13 lines ($1B = the 13-line center slice), so
   1383  fc38							; both endpoints open ⟺ the whole sprite is clear of that state.
   1384  fc38							; Ping-pong constants (#32/#4) = bank2 VcrCoveredState + CrunchClock
   1385  fc38							; (verify_build check_crunch_clock asserts the trio).
